        },
        "ImageDescription": {
          "value": "<p>Ferdinand Porsche saw the potential of an amphibious version of the VW Type 82 Kubelwagen. The German army was searching for a vehicle which would perform in difficult conditions such as snow, sand and mud. The project was the all wheel drive, boat shaped Type 128.\nThis vehicle was too large and unstable, a smaller Schwimmwagen was introduced, the Type 166. This design was a great success, simple mechanics and lightweight allowed the vehicle to traverse difficult terrain with ease, not to mention outstanding amphibious capabilities.\nEngine; 20hp 1131cc flat 4 cylinder\n</p>\nPhotographed at the Southward Car Museum, Paraparaumu, NZ",
          "source": "commons-desc-page"
        },
